in the &quot;Cherubs are... not like children, like childhood, weird people&quot; sections but it feels like you're both concerned about being misunderstood while also circling around your points without cutting to the quick, which is what you need to do in these sections. You mention the idea of religious purity a few times, which I think is a very interesting angle but you only mention it in offhand ways. Basically, I get the vibe of what you're trying to say, but it needs to be much clearer than just vibes.<br /> <br /> Also in that section &quot;Philosophizing aside, Cherubs like youth...&quot; desperately needs some sort of clarity since it can easily be taken in some pretty dark ways.<br /> <br /> Minor typo, Aspiration begins with the sentence, &quot;Cherubs attain their condition.&quot; which feels like some editing fragment.<br /> <br /> I really like the section on the Glimmerside, you did a great job capturing what the Glimmerside is and evoking childhood wonder. I'm not sure if this is the chapter for clarifying things, but you mention some of it being a lens then kind of drop that language as the chapter moves on. It might make sense to jut stick to capturing the feeling of it here, and then getting into details in the rules chapter around which levels are like a perception filter and which are places you bodily go.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would like to thank you for taking the time to conduct an in-depth examination of the work. Truthfully, I was not expecting to get such a level of feedback. I will admit that I skimmed your post as I felt rather embarrassed, but I very much appreciate your commentary and criticism. Mechanically, the supplement is rather wonky and it can be difficult to perceive what the whole thrust of the splat is. There was a definite level of fatigue towards the end of the writing process, and the writing in some places is weak. I think this is especially apparent in the descriptions of some of the Enchantments and Charms.<br /> <br /> As an aside, it is true that the splat was intended for another audience. However, said audience rarely provides commentary, which was part of why I posted it here. I am thankful for the feedback I have been able to get thus far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28352-verlan","name":"Verlan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-22T02:00:14-08:00","id":1531278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verlan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1529679-cherub-the-longing#post1529679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I apologize if having the first post of an account be in regards to one's own work is in poor taste; I am not very aware of forum etiquette. In any case, thank you for your time.</div> </div> </div> </div><b><span style=\"color:#c0392b\">So from the </span><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\">forum rules</a>.</b><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rule 4</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Avoid advertising. </b>At the moderators\u2019 discretion, you can trade your Onyx Path or White Wolf books, but generally keep your posts to discussion, not promotion. Similarly, do not solicit donations. You may, however, discuss your own game design and creative projects unrelated to Onyx Path, provided you're not just using the forum as an advertising venue. Please use only a single thread in the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic\">Off Topic</a> forum. For game recruiting, please use a single thread in the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings\">Conventions, Gatherings, and Online Play</a> forum.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#c0392b\"><b>While you didn't ask or post anywhere else you do seem to be acting in good faith, aren't soliciting money and have a project relevant to Chronicles of Darkness fans so I'll transfer this thread to the Off Topic forum where it might attract some more attention. </b></span><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}